# Line endings: text files are LF in the repository AND in every working tree, on every platform.
# Without this a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true is Git for Windows' default) rewrites every text
# file to CRLF, and the Windows CI lane then fails tests that compare file contents — grammars, snippets,
# message catalogs and golden files are all read as bytes. Verified when this was added: every tracked
# text file was already LF in the index, so `git add --renormalize .` changes nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The one tracked file that is CRLF on purpose (cmd.exe batch files want it). Left byte-for-byte alone.
mvnw.cmd -text

# Binary files: never converted, never diffed as text. (text=auto would detect these by their NUL bytes;
# naming them means a new one cannot be misdetected.)
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jar binary
*.ttf binary
*.pdf binary
*.bin binary

# Sample corpus: preserve bytes verbatim and keep it out of language stats / diffs.
# The encoding/EOL samples MUST NOT be normalized by git (autocrlf, eol, BOM
# stripping) — that would destroy exactly what they exercise.
samples/encodings/** -text
samples/diff/conflict.txt -text
samples/** linguist-vendored
